Depends: libsane1 (>= 1.0.28) | libsane (>= 1.0.28), sane-utils
Recommends: simple-scan | skanlite | gscan2pdf | xsane
Installed-Size: @@INSTALLED_SIZE@@
Description: Driver enablement package for the Canon CanoScan LiDE 400 scanner
 Makes the CanoScan LiDE 400 USB flatbed scanner work on Ubuntu/Debian
 through SANE. The actual scanner driver is the SANE pixma backend
 shipped in libsane1 (support added in sane-backends 1.0.28); this
 package guarantees USB device permissions, disables USB autosuspend
 for the scanner, and ships usage/provenance documentation.
 .
 Includes udev rules for USB ID 04a9:1912 and a README with scanning
 instructions (scanimage, simple-scan). No proprietary Canon files
 are redistributed; everything in this package was authored from
 public SANE documentation and static analysis of the Windows
 driver installer.
